WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:01.537
Now we are ready to run the

00:00:01.563 --> 00:00:06.190
complete clinic schema This is an instructor-guided

00:00:06.216 --> 00:00:08.019
reference not a script you need to

00:00:08.045 --> 00:00:12.575
memorize Before clicking Run scan the script

00:00:12.601 --> 00:00:15.604
and count the CREATE TABLE statements Then

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:18.498
look for primary keys unique business identifiers

00:00:18.617 --> 00:00:22.826
foreign keys and check constraints Run the

00:00:22.853 --> 00:00:24.813
schema in the browser and confirm that

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:29.895
PostgreSQL creates the tables successfully The order

00:00:29.908 --> 00:00:32.211
matters because parent tables need to exist

00:00:32.224 --> 00:00:36.164
before child tables can reference them If

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:38.664
you copy the script into pgAdmin use

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:41.719
it as a reading exercise Trace each

00:00:41.746 --> 00:00:43.785
foreign key back to its parent table

00:00:45.622 --> 00:00:46.964
The main goal is to see how

00:00:46.977 --> 00:00:49.753
the conceptual and logical design decisions become

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:51.635
executable PostgreSQL
